   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "80c6b390",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-07-05T17:40:47.572912Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-07-05T17:40:47.572912Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-07-05T17:40:48.664818Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-07-05T17:40:48.664312Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import json\n",
    "import random\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "from collections import Counter\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "from PIL import Image\n",
    "\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.style.use(\"ggplot\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5ed82362",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Dataset Configuration"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "c39e784e",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-07-05T17:40:48.667874Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-07-05T17:40:48.666871Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-07-05T17:40:48.672975Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-07-05T17:40:48.672975Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Number of classes in cat_to_name.json : 102\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "DATASET_ROOT = Path(\"datasets/extracted/flower_data\")\n",
    "\n",
    "TRAIN_DIR = DATASET_ROOT / \"train\"\n",
    "VAL_DIR = DATASET_ROOT / \"valid\"\n",
    "TEST_DIR = DATASET_ROOT / \"test\"\n",
    "\n",
    "CAT_TO_NAME_PATH = DATASET_ROOT / \"cat_to_name.json\"\n",
    "\n",
    "with open(CAT_TO_NAME_PATH, encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n",
    "    cat_to_name = json.load(f)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Number of classes in cat_to_name.json : {len(cat_to_name)}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4f599a68",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Load Dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "### Dataset Loading\n",
    "\n",
    "Unlike the mushroom dataset, there's no ready-made CSV here: images are\n",
    "organized as `train/<class_id>/*.jpg` and `valid/<class_id>/*.jpg`.\n",
    "`class_id` is the folder name; the actual species name is looked up via\n",
    "`cat_to_name.json`.\n",
    "\n",
    "The `test/` folder is **unlabeled** (no subfolders, just a flat file list) —\n",
    "this comes from Oxford Flowers' original Udacity packaging, where the test\n",
    "set is provided without class labels. So `test_df` has no `label`/`class_id`\n",
    "column; the test set can only be used for path/integrity checks."
   ]
  },
  {
